    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Tax refund of \\$4,426.64.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Gross income} &= 989.60\\times52 = \\$51\\,459.20\\\\\\text{Deductions} &= 38.25\\times52+150 = \\$2\\,139\\\\\\text{Taxable income before rounding} &= 51\\,459.20-2\\,139 = \\$49\\,320.20\\\\\\text{Taxable income} &= \\$49\\,320\\quad\\text{(rounded down)}\\end{align*}$$\nThe taxable income is in the \\$45,001–\\$120,000 bracket.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Income tax} &= 5\\,092+0.325\\times(49\\,320-45\\,000)\\\\\\text{Income tax} &= \\$6\\,496.00\\\\\\text{Medicare levy} &= 0.02\\times49\\,320 = \\$986.40\\\\\\text{Total tax payable} &= 6\\,496.00+986.40 = \\$7\\,482.40\\\\\\text{Annual PAYG} &= 229.02\\times52 = \\$11\\,909.04\\\\\\text{Refund} &= 11\\,909.04-7\\,482.40 = \\$4\\,426.64\\end{align*}$$\nPAYG exceeds total tax payable, so Liam receives a tax refund.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
